#
# holt — Terraform for a ctags that has no Terraform parser.
#
# Loaded ONLY when holt has measured that this toolchain cannot extract Terraform symbols.
# universal-ctags gained a Terraform parser in 6.x; Ubuntu 24.04 LTS ships 5.9.0, so on the
# most common Linux install holt would otherwise report "no symbols" for every .tf file and,
# because silence reads as "nothing there", quietly claim two agents editing the same
# infrastructure had nothing in common.
#
# Never loaded on a ctags that already has the parser — --langdef would collide with it.
#
--langdef=Terraform
--map-Terraform=+.tf
--map-Terraform=+.tfvars
--kinddef-Terraform=r,resource,resources
--kinddef-Terraform=d,data,data sources
--kinddef-Terraform=v,variable,variables
--kinddef-Terraform=o,output,outputs
--kinddef-Terraform=m,module,modules
--kinddef-Terraform=p,provider,providers
--regex-Terraform=/^[ \t]*resource[ \t]+"[^"]+"[ \t]+"([^"]+)"/\1/r/
--regex-Terraform=/^[ \t]*data[ \t]+"[^"]+"[ \t]+"([^"]+)"/\1/d/
--regex-Terraform=/^[ \t]*variable[ \t]+"([^"]+)"/\1/v/
--regex-Terraform=/^[ \t]*output[ \t]+"([^"]+)"/\1/o/
--regex-Terraform=/^[ \t]*module[ \t]+"([^"]+)"/\1/m/
--regex-Terraform=/^[ \t]*provider[ \t]+"([^"]+)"/\1/p/
